{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And Joseph wept when they spoke to him.</b> As soon as they mentioned his father to him, he wept out of the greatness of his love, and his compassion was stirred. And behold, his brothers asked him for forgiveness, but Scripture did not explain that he forgave them. And our Rabbis of blessed memory already explained that whoever sins against his fellow and repents is never forgiven until he appeases his fellow. And even though Scripture mentions ״וינחם אותם וידבר על לבם״ — 'and he comforted them and spoke to their heart' — which appears to show that they found favor with Joseph, nevertheless we do not see that Scripture mentions forgiveness on Joseph's part, nor that he grants them that he will bear their transgression and their sin. If so, they died in their punishment without Joseph's forgiveness, and it is impossible for their sin to be atoned except through his forgiveness. Therefore the punishment needed to be stored away and sealed to be exacted after a time, in the matter of the Ten Martyrs of the Kingdom." "<b>And it seems</b> to me that there is a hint of this in Scripture, from the fact that the expression is doubled, making two parts of it: 'the transgression of your brothers' and 'their sin' — 'the transgression of the servants of the God of your father,' when Scripture ought to have said, 'And now, please bear their transgression.'" "<b>Rather,</b> Scripture intended to hint: if you bear the transgression of your brothers and their sin, then the transgression of the servants of the God of your father will be forgiven. And Scripture explained that 'the transgression of the servants of the God of his father' is the transgression of his brothers, for the Holy One, blessed be He, will recall their earlier sins to them. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :register {:flags {1 ["God"], 2 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:00.016102648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}